Autonomy: **{{ autonomy.default }}** by default.
`L1` writes a report and commits nothing · `L2` commits to a branch for review · `L3` merges.

Start at L1 and stay there for a week. The point of week one is not shipped work — it is
finding out which gates are badly specified, and you learn that by reading diffs.

## 2. Topology

The agent that writes the code does not decide whether it is done. That separation is the
whole reason the loop can be left alone.

```
trigger -> read STATE.md -> pick next unit -> isolated worktree
        -> implementer writes -> verifier checks -> gates green?
             yes: record, act per autonomy level
             no:  inject failure text, try again, unless a stop rule fires
```

