## 4. Stop rules

| Rule | Threshold | Action |
|---|---|---|
| Success | all blocking gates green | act per autonomy level, record, exit 0 |
| Attempt ceiling | {{ stop.max_attempts }} | halt, escalate with every attempt's output |
| No progress | same failure {{ stop.no_progress }} times | halt — the agent is stuck on a signal it cannot act on. From outside this looks identical to persistence, which is why it needs its own rule |
| Denylist touch | any | hard stop, no commit, page a human |

## 5. What the loop may not touch

If the agent can edit what it is judged against, the shortest path to "done" is to lower the
bar — and it will find that path. Checked *before* verification runs, in `gate.yaml`.

{% for d in deny %}- `{{ d }}`
{% endfor %}
## 6. State

`STATE.md` is the spine. Every attempt starts from a clean context and rebuilds its brief
from that file plus the failing gate text, rather than carrying a conversation forward. The
agent forgets between runs; the repository does not.

